# --- ETK PROJECT GITIGNORE ---

# 1. Ignore the Shader Vault (Relative paths)
# This stops those massive .dat and .SELF files from hitting GitHub
vault/
**/vault/

# 1b. Ignore the Tier-B host snapshot tree (addendum: install.sh backs up
# rig-side telemetry ledgers, tuned RPCS3 configs, and the RPCS3 user-profile
# tree — saves, trophies, .rap licenses — here on every install run).
# Mirrors the vault/ precedent: never auto-deleted, never committed.
state/
**/state/

# 1c. Belt-and-suspenders guard: the operator-friendly `screenshots/` is
# a symlink to `state/screenshots/` (see addendum convention — Tier-B
# mutable state lives under `state/`). If someone deletes the symlink
# and recreates a real dir by accident, this keeps PNG captures out of
# the repo regardless.
/screenshots
/screenshots/

# 2. Ignore Live Data / Shared Memory
# We don't want to track etk_mode.txt or the command queue
shm/
**/shm/

# 2b. Probe capture output — scripts/etk_probe.sh writes timestamped CSVs to
# $ETK_ROOT/etk_probe at runtime (thermal-calibration sweeps). Runtime data,
# same precedent as vault/ and state/ — never committed. The historical
# 20260521 captures were archived under _archive/etk_probe/ (also ignored).
etk_probe/
**/etk_probe/

# 3. macOS Pollution
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*

# 4. System & Editor Caches
*.log
*.tmp
*.swp
__pycache__/
.vscode/

# 5 Ignore the dev _archive
_archive/
/os-install

# 6. Operator config — generated locally by install.sh's first-run
# wizard. Tracks the rig SSH target, build tier, HUD preferences, etc.
# The canonical template is `etk.conf.example` (committed).
etk.conf

# 7. Claude Code machine-local settings — personal, not shared. The `.claude/`
# dir stays at the project root (Claude Code requires it there); only the
# per-machine local settings file is untracked.
.claude/settings.local.json
